  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Keep the ball – 3v1 in two zones",
  "description": "Two teams and two zones next to each other. Start with 3v1 in one zone: the blue team passes to keep the ball, and one red player tries to win it. The other reds wait in the second zone.\n\nWhen the red player wins the ball, they carry it over to their zone, where their team-mates are waiting. The blue team then sends one player across as the new defender, and now it is red who keeps the ball. Adjust the numbers and the size of the zones to the level. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Move so the player on the ball always has two options."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Pass past the defender, not straight at them."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Whoever wins the ball: get over to your zone quickly."
    }
  ],
